Oh, right, it's Debian... apache conf files are different. Sorry for that!

Anyway, I don't think it's smart to disclose your apache conf in it's entirety =/

You have to create modR.conf and modR.load files in mods-enabled folder, just take a look at the other files. I'm not running a Debian distro (I'm using Arch FWIW), but I'll take a look at Debian in my VM. But you should try to install it on your own, it's not that hard, .load and .conf files have very simple structure. You basically have to put a few Apache directives in each one. Unfortunately, I don't recall the exact procedure... =/

Good luck! ;-)

