> conf file.
>
> <Location /RApacheInfo>
>         SetHandler r-info
> </Location>
>
> <Directory /var/www/R-files>
>         SetHandler r-script
>         RHandler sys.source
> </Directory>
>
> then try with a simple .R code in R-files folder, u will definitely
> get the result
>
> Next thing to do is installing brew - u might be facing problems with brew
> installation
>
> For installing brew, go to terminal and change the permissions of the
> following folder as R through apache directly checks the the following
> folder for the packages
>
> sudo chmod a+rwx /usr/local/lib/R/site-library
>
> then go to R through terminal and install the brew package using the code
>

> *install.packages("brew", lib="/usr/lib/R/site-library")*
>
> then go to *sudo etc/apache2/apache2.conf* file  and copy paste the code

>
> <Directory /var/www/brew>
>         SetHandler r-script
>         RHandler brew::brew
> </Directory>
>
> Now in that brew folder go with that example in jeroens lecture.
>
