Arjun, I'm affraid you have a typo here:

> I typed the code in the terminal sudo etc/apache2/apache2.conf to get the configuration

perhaps you meant: sudo gedit /etc/apache2/apache2.conf
or emacs/vim/nano/kate/whatever... instead of gedit...

Anyway, thanks for thorough explanation. I'm not using Debian distro for a while now, so I was unaware of Jeff's RApache package for Ubuntu. IMHO, by putting this in apache2.conf:

<Directory /var/www/brew>
	SetHandler r-script
	RHandler brew::brew
</Directory>

you'll get a bunch of problems, since all the files within /var/www/brew are processed with brew::brew. Try using <FilesMatch> directive, and match the files you'd like to process with brew with a regular expression. For basic stuff, however, this config is just fine...

